# Carried patch: run SandboxSnapshot commit/unpause Jobs in a dedicated namespace.
#
# Upstream: https://github.com/alibaba/OpenSandbox
# Base commit: e95681e791b33b3893033940cbeaa5ab192bf21b (main, 2026-08-02)
# Why: the snapshot commit/unpause Jobs hostPath-mount the node containerd
# socket. OpenSandbox creates them in the SandboxSnapshot's own (tenant)
# namespace, where bex enforces PodSecurity "baseline" — the commit pod is
# rejected and pause hangs (ADR042 D5, found w3/m32/t007). This patch adds a
# --snapshot-job-namespace controller flag: when set, (1) the privileged Jobs
# run in that one platform namespace (cross-namespace owner references being
# invalid, Job→snapshot linkage moves to labels and cleanup keeps the existing
# TTL + explicit-delete paths), and (2) snapshot repositories nest under the
# sandbox's source namespace (<registry>/<namespace>/<sandbox>-<container>) so
# registry pull ACLs can be scoped per tenant — the prerequisite for w3/m42
# t002's per-workspace resume-pull credentials. Empty flag = byte-identical
# upstream behavior (same-namespace Jobs, flat repository layout).
# Upstreaming: intended as a PR to alibaba/OpenSandbox; drop this file when a
# release containing it is pinned. Tracking: .pm/w3/m42 (docs/ADR047 gap 2).
#
# git apply runs from the upstream repo root (paths are kubernetes/...).
